[COMMENTS]
STATION,One of the Balquhidder experimental catchments. GENERAL: Aluminium alloy Flat V (1:10) weir, 3.2m wide with vertical sidewalls, keyed into a natural rockbar. Station added to peak flows dataset in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7). STATION HYDROMETRY: Containable head 1.2m has max. flow of 9.0 cumecs. FLOW RECORD: Instrumentation problems throughout 1996, data infilled from Lower Monachyle and Kirkton. FLOW REGIME: Natural catchment.
CATCHMENT,Very wet interfluve area to the break in slope to a steep- sided glacial valley. Shallow and deep peat, peaty gleys and upland brown earths over mica schist. Some bare rock on W boundary. Heather moorland. Experimental catchment run by IH, nested within 18017 and neighbouring 18018.
Qmed Suitability,Flows based on weir equation only.
Pooling Suitability,Flows based on weir equation only.
[END]
